  "description": "AGSC-06-44 with AGSC-06-08: at Level 2 and above the rel#surface link of the chunks surface carries digest (over /chunks.jsonl), agsc-chunk-count and agsc-chunk-set, and validate-wellknown recomputes them over the fetched file and requires them of a document whose agsc-spec-version is 1.1.0 or later. (1) complete: a 1.1.0 document whose chunks link carries the three, over a chunks file of three lines (the export of chk-0014): valid. (2) missing: the same 1.1.0 document without the three: the checker reports AGSC-E202, the code for a required member that is absent. (3) earlier-document: a document that declares 1.0.0 and has no chunks digest: valid, because the attributes are required only of 1.1.0 and later. The files input holds the bytes the checker fetches for each route; every digest in the documents is the SHA-256 of those bytes, so the valid documents recompute. Derived by hand with hashlib.",
